          "level": 1,
          "content": "Chapter – 2 Arithmetic Expressions"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.226,
            0.239,
            0.245
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 24**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.259,
            0.852,
            0.298
          ],
          "content": "**Choose your favourite number and write as many expressions as you can having that value.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.313,
            0.453,
            0.33
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** Let us choose the number 24."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.328,
            0.859,
            0.409
          ],
          "content": "The arithmetic expressions for the number can be as follows: 12 + 12 = 24; 4 × 6 = 24; 48 ÷ 2 = 24, 34 – 10 = 24, 20 + 4 = 24 etc. Now you choose your number and form arithmetic expressions for that number."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.424,
            0.24,
            0.443
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 25**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.457,
            0.279,
            0.475
          ],
          "content": "**Figure it Out**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.476,
            0.878,
            0.564
          ],
          "content": "**1. Fill in the blanks to make the expressions equal on both sides of the = sign:** (a) 13 + 4 = \\_ \\_ + 6 (b) 22 + = 6 × 5 (c) 8 × = 64 ÷ 2 (d) 34 – = 25"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.578,
            0.518,
            0.597
          ],
          "content": "**Ans: 1.** (a) 11 (b) 8 (c) 4 (d) 9"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.611,
            0.875,
            0.699
          ],
          "content": "**2. Arrange the following expressions in ascending (increasing) order of their values. (a) 67 – 19 (b) 67 – 20 (c) 35 + 25 (d) 5 × 11 (e) 120 ÷ 3**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.713,
            0.64,
            0.731
          ],
          "content": "**Ans: 2.** 120 ÷ 3 < 67 – 20 < 67 – 19 < 5 × 11 < 35 + 25"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.747,
            0.24,
            0.766
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 26**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.78,
            0.882,
            0.858
          ],
          "content": "？ **Use ‘>’ or ‘<’ ‘=’ in each of the following expressions to compare them. Can you do it without complicated calculations? Explain your thinking in each case. Ans:** (a) > (b) = (c) < (d) < (e) <"
        },
        {
